Verify again every time the workspace changes, until interrupted

Usage: njutest watch [OPTIONS] [-- <TEST ARGS>...]

Arguments:
  [TEST ARGS]...
          Arguments for the test binaries. Only the flags njutest does not own are allowed:
          --test-threads, --include-ignored, --nocapture, --show-output

Options:
      --poll-ms <MS>
          How often to ask the workspace whether it changed. 500 by default

      --directory <DIR>
          The workspace to verify. The working directory by default

      --config <PATH>
          The configuration file. `.njutest.toml` beside the workspace by default; a missing one is
          the defaults

  -p, --package <NAME>
          Verify only this package. Repeatable; the default is every member

      --ui <UI>
          How to write progress

          Possible values:
          - plain:     Lines a person reads
          - jsonl:     One JSON object per line, for a program
          - dashboard: One block that says where the run is, rewritten in place
          
          [default: plain]

      --format <FORMAT>
          What to write when the run is over. The default is the drawing at a terminal and the
          record stream anywhere else

          Possible values:
          - lines: The record stream
          - json:  The canonical document, exactly as the run wrote it
          - spec:  What the seams the run watched observed the system doing, and who holds each
            sentence up
          - human: What a person reads: the source, with every place the tests do not see marked on
            it
          - agent: A briefing for something that will act on this without a screen, as Markdown

      --trace[=<DIR>]
          Record what the run does, under DIR or `.njutest/trace/<run>`

      --keep-temp
          Keep the directories the run worked in

      --offline
          Pass --offline to every cargo command

      --locked
          Pass --locked to every cargo command

      --no-cache
          Establish everything afresh instead of reading back what an earlier run of the same inputs
          established

      --changed
          Mutate only the files that differ from a revision. `CHANGE_ASSURED` is the most this can
          conclude

      --changed-from <REV>
          The revision to compare against. Implies --changed

      --faults
          Fail every call a `?` asks about, one at a time, and say which failures the suite noticed.
          Wins over `[faults] inject`

      --shard <K/N>
          Judge only one part of the catalog, as `K/N`. Every part measures the whole baseline;
          `njutest merge` combines what they judged

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
